# Copyright header

## Existing Chromium / Skia / third-party files

Files that already say **The Chromium Authors**, **The Android Open Source Project**, or another upstream notice **keep that notice**. Do not rewrite them to The Mogu Authors. Do not bump their year as a drive-by.

## New files this repo authors

For **new** engineering files that are not upstream snapshots (docs under `docs/`, `.cursor/rules` `.mdc`, `.cursor/skills`, new scripts you add):

```text
Copyright (c) YYYY The Mogu Authors.
All rights reserved.
```

- `YYYY` is the **current calendar year**.
- C/C++: `//` comments. Python/shell: `#`. Markdown / `.mdc`: HTML comment **after** YAML frontmatter. Shebang scripts: header immediately after `#!`.

## Don’t

- Don’t stamp Mogu copyright onto `ui/`, `base/`, `skia/`, or `third_party/` files that already have an upstream header.
- Don’t copy a stale year from another file.
